   159	/// Embedders wanting a stricter rule check
   160	/// `input.paste.isSafe` themselves before calling. A paste event never
   161	/// puts the data on the input stream, so the rule doesn't apply to it.
   162	///
   163	/// The contents are read at most once per call and buffered whole, so
   164	/// the source needs no stability across reads. Nothing reaches the
   165	/// writer until the read completed and the text passed the rule:
   166	/// every error writes nothing, and a failed event records no grant.
   167	pub fn paste(ctx: Context, req: Request) Error!bool {
   168	    // If the source is a clipboard and mode 5522 is enabled and
   169	    // the caller can handle kitty events, then do a kitty event.
